(A major outstanding question in neuroscience is whether the neocortex us\es the same powerful learning )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 567.9 Tm
(algorithm as current AI models: error backpropagation. One way this coul\d be accomplished is as a )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 554.4 Tm
(function of the temporal derivative \(i.e., differences in neural activi\ty states over time\), which can closely )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 540.9 Tm
(approximate the backpropagated error gradient. We tested the hypothesis \that the direction of synaptic )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 527.4 Tm
(plasticity is a function of the temporal derivative in synaptic activity\ over the course of a 200 ms \(5 Hz\) )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 513.9 Tm
(theta cycle. Using mouse hippocampal slices, we drove presynaptic activi\ty across the two 100 ms halves )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 500.4 Tm
(of a 200 ms window at either 25 Hz or 50 Hz, combined with corresponding\ low and high magnitudes of )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 486.9 Tm
(postsynaptic depolarization, testing all four 2x2 combinations of these \low and high activity levels, while )Tj
