/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 473.4 Tm
(measuring the resulting effects on synaptic efficacy \(as measured by EP\SP amplitude to standard test )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 459.9 Tm
(probes\). Consistent with the computational hypothesis, a positive tempo\ral derivative \(low to high\) resulted )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 446.4 Tm
(in LTP \(increased synaptic strength\), while a negative temporal deriva\tive \(high to low\) resulted in LTD. )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 432.9 Tm
(Critically, both no-change conditions \(stable low or high across 200 ms\\) resulted in no net synaptic change, )Tj
ET
BT
/T1_0 24 Tf
0.45 0 0 0.45 72 419.4 Tm
(even though the high no-change condition had the highest overall synapti\c activity levels. Possible )Tj
